notes/screenshots/_inbox/
# data/market/holdings_inbox/ is NO LONGER ignored (his call, 2026-10-06).
# The old reason — "the file is only the delivery and can be downloaded
# again any time" — is false twice over, and both halves were proven on
# 2026-10-05/06:
#
#   * Each file is a DATED SNAPSHOT. You can download today's holdings; you
#     cannot download the ones behind a row dated 2026-10-02. Losing the
#     file loses the provenance of every figure parsed out of it.
#   * Seven of the nine issuers he holds block automated download entirely,
#     so "again any time" means him, by hand, on nine websites.
#
# And the cost of losing them is not theoretical: a refresh with the files
# missing sends every fund to a ten-name floor (guarded in
# fetch_holdings(), but the guard exists because the loss is plausible).
# 812 KB for the lot. The repo is private; these are the issuers' own
# published holdings, no account data of his in them.
*.pdf
*.xlsx
*.xls
.env

# Transient sync backups (e.g., data/positions.csv.bak)
*.bak

# Jupyter
.ipynb_checkpoints/
*.ipynb_checkpoints

# `data/screens/` and `notes/alerts/` used to be ignored here. Both are gone
# (Phase 2e): the screen images were regenerable and were deleted, and the 46
# daily alert files moved to `_archive/alerts/` and are now COMMITTED — being
# ignored meant the only record of how close each stop came to firing lived on
# one laptop with no backup.

# Machine scratch space for planned work: brainstorm mockups, the execution
# ledger for a plan in flight, and per-commit review diffs. All regenerable,
# none of it a record Yaron reads.
.superpowers/

# The built portfolio page: machine output, regenerated in seconds by
# ops/build_page.py, and it would change on every sync (spec D11).
ops/portfolio.html
